Z||000000||phillip||07-02-2000||02:54 PM||||<BR>i originaly started this topic in general fiero topics crying over my car and ending up asking tech questions so i guess i'll switch it to tech.<P>my '87 started running really rough and tgowens told me about the scan tool at auto zone. it may have worked. the car for whatever reason started running a little better but i tried the tool any way and got a code for my idle speed control. couldn't get anything out of it with the 9v battery test (might have tested the wrong terminals and shorted it out or something), so i replaced it. for the moment it seems to be back to it's usual sputter (i hate that engine).  i only drove it a little so the ecm could set the control as instructed.<P>ok, thats not what this post is about. before i used the scan tool on my '87, i tried it on my indy just in case i did it wrong since i haven't started driving it anyway. got codes 45 and 42. 45 is o2 sensor and/or circuit. 42 is not in the book. anyone know what it is. thanks for any help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||RobertVol||07-02-2000||03:06 PM||||I believe it has something to do with Spark timing. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||07-02-2000||04:18 PM||||phillip, try this -- Code 42 - Electronic Spark Timing<P>If the vehicle will not start and run, check the wire leading to terminal 12 of the ECM. Check the EST wire (terminal 19 of the<BR>ECM) leading to the HEI module (terminal E). Check all distributor wires. Check the wire leading from EST terminal A to<BR>ECM terminal 12, and the wire from EST terminal A to ECM terminal 3. Replace the HEI module. Note this service bulletin<BR>regarding code 42. <P>this came from here...... <A HREF="http://www.tg-2000.com/Fiero/codes.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tg-2000.com/Fiero/codes.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||phillip||07-02-2000||11:05 PM||||thanks. i'll look at that. the car dose run though,but rough.<P>also took the '87 for a longer drive. got caught in the park crusin' traffic jam,bit of city drivin', and a couple of miles on the expressway. seems ok,or as good as it gets.||||reg||1
